window.__finlexDocLoaded(10146,{"id":10146,"articles":[{"id":1000579,"no":"Overview","heading":"Scope & Key Requirements (Public Summary)","text":"Sets out the coordinated 15% global minimum tax framework (Income Inclusion Rule — IIR, Undertaxed Profits Rule — UTPR, and Qualified Domestic Minimum Top-up Tax — QDMTT) for MNE groups with consolidated revenue ≥ EUR 750 million. Directly linked to IAS 12 Pillar Two amendments.","seq":0},{"id":1000580,"no":"GloBE Art. 1–10","heading":"15% Global Minimum Tax: Scope, ETR Formula & Charging Order","text":"• Scope (Art. 1.1): MNE groups with consolidated revenue ≥ EUR 750 million in at least 2 of the 4 preceding fiscal years.\n• Jurisdictional Effective Tax Rate (ETR) (Art. 5.1–5.2): Adjusted Covered Taxes ÷ Net GloBE Income per jurisdiction; if ETR < 15%, Top-up Tax Percentage = 15% − ETR applied to Excess Profit (Net GloBE Income minus Substance-based Income Exclusion for payroll & tangible assets).\n• Charging rule order: (1) Qualified Domestic Minimum Top-up Tax (QDMTT) collected locally first; (2) Income Inclusion Rule (IIR) at Ultimate Parent Entity; (3) Undertaxed Profits Rule (UTPR) backstop.\n• Transitional CbCR Safe Harbours & IAS 12 link: temporary safe harbours simplify 2024–2026 compliance; accounting follows IAS 12.4A/88A–88D mandatory deferred tax exception.","seq":1},{"id":1000581,"no":"Official Access","heading":"Official Handbook & Reference Entry","text":"Official source (OECD): https://www.oecd.org/en/topics/sub-issues/global-minimum-tax/global-anti-base-erosion-model-rules-pillar-two.html\nStatus: in_force. Detailed paragraph-level summaries and practice notes can be expanded incrementally.","seq":2}]});
